# n8n + Willow — copy vars into your n8n process environment
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where this file goes depends on HOW you start n8n:
#
# A) Monorepo:  cd .../n8n && pnpm start
#    → dotenv loads from the CLI working directory:
#    → copy these lines into:  n8n/packages/cli/bin/.env
#
# B) npx:        cd some-folder && npx n8n
#    → put .env in that same folder (cwd when you run the command)
#
# C) Any method: export vars in your shell before starting n8n
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Willow base URL (no trailing slash). Used by the sample workflow URL expression.
WILLOW_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# Optional — n8n defaults are usually fine for local GUI exploration
# N8N_PORT=5678
# WEBHOOK_URL=http://localhost:5678/

# Optional — set if your admin enables env blocking in nodes
# (leave unset so HTTP Request expressions can read $env.WILLOW_BASE_URL)
# N8N_BLOCK_ENV_ACCESS_IN_NODE=false

# Recommended for non-throwaway installs (stable credential encryption)
# openssl rand -hex 32
# N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
